{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" packs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unpacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" macro generates a separate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" class for each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":" property. A view reading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"text":" won’t re-render when only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates the observer class tree and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","type":"heading","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reducer Weight","type":"heading","anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Effect Threading","type":"heading","anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use async alternatives: ","type":"text"},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + continuation instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", async file I\/O instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the a